    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d193">

                <pb facs="0345" n="173" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg173"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 857.857/94</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Rotterdam</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Krogh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rotterdam</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 13, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 9 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Norwegian freight steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Thode Fagesund</hi> of
                    Tonsberg, Norway, owned by Wilhelm Wilhelmsen, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">en route</hi> from Falmouth to Rotterdam, with cargo
                    sesame seed from Shanghai, having one American aboard, namely Ruff us
                        Alfonso Bennett (colored, cook, born Hampton, Va.,
                    formerly served U. S. Navy) stopped, torpedoed, sunk by German submarine
                    afternoon March 11 in North Sea, 2° 58′ eastern longitude and 51° 54′ northern
                    latitude. All officers, crew, consisting 28 men including
                        Bennett, were given 10 minutes to enter boats and were
                    saved. All were picked up from boats in calm sea after 12 hours by Dutch lugger
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Judana;</hi> were later transferred to Dutch lugger
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Vlaardingen</hi> and brought safely to Rotterdam. Am
                    mailing Bennett’s affidavit and endeavoring obtain copies
                    affidavits officers, crew, from Norwegian Consul.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Krogh</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
